/*
 * hello-tutorial-gap.compact
 *
 * Lab copy of the published getting-started Hello World contract.
 * Source: https://docs.midnight.network/getting-started/hello-world
 * Upstream gap: https://github.com/midnightntwrk/midnight-docs/issues/1396
 *
 * The published sample is only this pragma, one public Opaque<"string">
 * ledger field, and storeMessage. Circuit arguments are private. disclose()
 * is required before the public write. The tutorial deploys with
 * `yarn test:local` on the Docker devnet and does not show a witness,
 * a ledger read-back, or the Preprod path (`yarn proof:up` /
 * `yarn test:preprod` lives on /guides/deploy-mn-app, not on this page).
 *
 * Do not add a getter circuit here. Public ledger reads are off-chain.
 * Do not invent a witness API; witnesses are declared in the election and
 * bulletin-board examples, not in this tutorial.
 *
 * Pins: Compact ~0.31.1 / language 0.23, midnight-js 4.1.1,
 * DApp Connector 4.0.1, proof-server 8.1.0.
 * This file does not deploy and does not fix the public indexer or node.
